{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 19,
  "title": "Around the house",
  "description": "Name the furniture, and use the plural when there is more than one.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Furniture is a closed list of nouns, and every one of them needs its article. This unit also does the work of the plural, because a room rarely has only one chair.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "El sofá, el sillón and el biombo are masculine. La estantería, la cómoda, la repisa and la alfombra are feminine. La planta is a nice one to know: it means both the plant and the floor of a building, and the context tells you which one you mean.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "el sofá",
            "en": "the sofa"
          },
          {
            "es": "la estantería",
            "en": "the bookcase"
          },
          {
            "es": "la planta",
            "en": "the plant"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "More than one",
        "body": "The plural of a noun adds -s, or -es when the noun ends in a vowel: el sillón becomes los sillones and la planta becomes las plantas. The articles change too: el becomes los and la becomes las. So one sofa is el sofá, and two sofas are los sofás.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "los sillones",
            "en": "the armchairs"
          },
          {
            "es": "las plantas",
            "en": "the plants"
          },
          {
            "es": "dos sofás",
            "en": "two sofas"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
